---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '@/components/PageHero.astro';
import { systemState } from '@/lib/system-state';
---

<BaseLayout title="System state" description="Canonical, evidence-based capability and availability status for Super ii.">
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="What is available now 🧭"
    title="Super ii system state"
    description={`Snapshot ${systemState.snapshot}. See what has been built, what is available now, and the evidence behind each capability.`}
    compact
  >
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="button button--dark" href="/system-state.json">View JSON</a>
      <a class="button button--secondary" href="/system-state.md">View Markdown</a>
    </div>
  </PageHero>

  <main class="section shell system-state-page">
    <section class="repository-section">
      <div class="repository-section__heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Evidence register</p><h2>Capabilities</h2></div>
        <span>{systemState.capabilities.length} tracked</span>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-scroll">
        <table class="comparison-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Capability</th><th>Status</th><th>Availability</th><th>Evidence and boundary</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {systemState.capabilities.map((item) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">{item.capability}</th>
                <td><code>{item.status}</code></td>
                <td>{item.availability}</td>
                <td>{item.evidence}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="repository-section">
      <div class="repository-section__heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Shared vocabulary</p><h2>Status ladder</h2></div></div>
      <ol class="status-ladder">
        {systemState.statusLadder.map((status, index) => <li><span>{index + 1}</span><code>{status}</code></li>)}
      </ol>
      <p>If a required check is unavailable, Super ii treats that capability as unavailable instead of skipping the check. The public MCP endpoint is read-only; compute, publishing, private data, and payments are outside its authority.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
